WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.270
Congress votes to spend 100 billion
dollars on new highways and bridges.

2
00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:07.730
Crews are hired, concrete is poured,

3
00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:09.630
and the paychecks go out.

4
00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:11.740
But when economists add it all up,

5
00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:16.070
real GDP can rise by a
multiple of that 100 billion.

6
00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:18.770
So how can 1 dollar of
government spending raise

7
00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:21.880
real GDP by more than 1 dollar?

8
00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:27.490
In this mission, you'll calculate the spending
multiplier from the marginal propensity to consume.

9
00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:30.210
Then you'll compare it
with the tax multiplier,

10
00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.430
and find out which one is bigger.

11
00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:35.490
Your mission: find out
how 1 dollar of spending

12
00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:38.430
can add more than 1 dollar to real GDP.
